<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="obsidian-fragments">
<span class="c6">Obsidian Fragments for Frost Death Knight DPS Phase 4</span></h3>In the new Inferno Protocol Dungeon: Twilight difficulty, bosses will drop <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a>s, which can be used to purchase T12 items and LFR-versions of Dragon Soul-gear. Many of the items listed in this guide, will be sourced from here, making these dungeons instrumental in getting you up to speed for Dragon Soul raiding. You will find them listed in the guide, along with their prices. Some of these items are even better than the Heroic versions of Firelands gear - particularly trinkets and weapons.<br/>
<br/>If you are coming into Inferno Protocol: Twilight dungeons, it is not advised to spend <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a>s on the slightly cheaper Firelands-tier pieces. The new T13 is only slightly more expensive and is more powerful than Normal Firelands gear.<br/>
<br/>
